# Bond dumps carry real key material (LinkKey, LTK, IRK, CSRK). The tool writes
# them under these names; none of them is ever a commit. This is the single
# most important line in this file -- the repo's whole subject matter is secret
# by nature.
*.bond
*.bonds
bonds/
dump-*.json
*-keys.json
*-keys.txt

# Registry exports, in case someone reaches for reg.exe /y by hand.
*.reg
*.hiv
SYSTEM
SYSTEM.*

# HCI captures from `btbond-sync.py --capture-hci`. What the tool wants out of
# them (remote version/features) is device capability, not secret -- but a
# capture that happens to span a PAIRING records key distribution over the
# air, and nothing in the filename tells you which kind you have.
*.btmon.log
remote-info.json

# BlueZ state copied out for inspection.
info
var-lib-bluetooth/

# Extensions that can hold secrets. Nothing matches today; accident insurance.
*.env
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
# Paketleme çıktısı — `pip install .` ve `python -m build` üretiyor.
build/
dist/

# Editor / OS
*.swp
.DS_Store
